    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} \\right\\rceil\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify the expression inside the square root.\n2. Calculate the square root.\n3. Apply the negative sign.\n4. Apply the ceiling function.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail.\n\n1. Simplify the expression inside the square root:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{49}{4} = 12.25\n   \\]\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = \\sqrt{12.25}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the square root:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{12.25} = 3.5\n   \\]\n   So, we have:\n   \\[\n   -\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = -3.5\n   \\]\n\n3. Apply the negative sign:\n   \\[\n   -3.5\n   \\]\n\n4. Apply the ceiling function:\n   The ceiling function \\(\\left\\lceil x \\right\\rceil\\) is the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(x\\). For \\(x = -3.5\\), the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(-3.5\\) is \\(-3\\). Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil -3.5 \\right\\rceil = -3\n   \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
