    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "First, we start by finding the value of the expression inside the ceiling function, which is $-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}$.\n\nWe know that $\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}}$ can be simplified as follows:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n-\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}} = -\\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to apply the ceiling function, denoted by $\\lceil \\cdot \\rceil$, to $-\\frac{7}{2}$. The ceiling function returns the smallest integer greater than or equal to the given number. Since $-\\frac{7}{2} = -3.5$, the smallest integer greater than or equal to $-3.5$ is $-3$. Therefore:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil -\\frac{7}{2} \\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil -3.5 \\right\\rceil = -3\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
